{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And he shall take a handful.</b> From the root לקמצים, and our ancestors interpreted קמץ as 'kamatz gadol,' and their words are true." "<b>Of its fine flour.</b> A small amount of it, and likewise of the oil; only all the frankincense shall be burned." "<b>Its memorial portion.</b> The alef is added, and the meaning is: that which serves him as a remembrance before HaShem on account of his meal-offering. And many interpreted it like 'fragrance and incense,' as in זכרו כיין לבנון (his fragrance is like the wine of Lebanon)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:08:27.063794405Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}